Wine asks for Wine Mono 11.3.0, the version Wine's master branch asks for.

From upstream Wine (wine-mirror/wine, LGPL-2.1-or-later): Wine's own version-bump commits from Wine Mono
10.4.1 (the version CrossOver 26.3.0 asks for) to 11.3.0, carried unchanged in this order. They came after
CrossOver 26.3.0 and apply to it with no fuzz; this file is their combined diff:

- 76743968cc8aadc54c8b4e34c9b465e40f10f0fb, Esme Povirk: "mscoree: Update Wine Mono to 11.0.0."
- 9f4295cec027d260c39fcf167b063acd939e5fc6, Esme Povirk: "mscoree: Update Wine Mono to 11.1.0."
- 2927904de2dc9c69bc1bd60a45c0839dad60eed9, Esme Povirk: "mscoree: Update Wine Mono to 11.2.0."
- 2142f7724d7ea9b34fe71711fb83952e887d431f, Esme Povirk: "appwiz.cpl: Move architecture to
  addon_info_t." Wine Mono 11.3.0 has its own architecture names (x86, arm64), so 29a87db needs it.
- 29a87db3c71d9cc7e4c20fa44eb813172c0e11a9, Esme Povirk: "mscoree: Update Wine Mono to 11.3.0."

Each commit changes the version and its SHA-256 in dlls/appwiz.cpl/addons.c, the version mscoree expects
in dlls/mscoree/mscoree_private.h, and the version Wine's own CI uses in tools/gitlab/test.yml.

Why mavrik needs it: the engine carries the Wine Mono its tree asks for (the addons gate checks they are
the same), and Wine Mono 11 brings FNA 26.08 and SDL 3.4.14 for XNA and FNA games, and WPF, System.Drawing
and Visual Basic 6 fixes. Remove when the pinned CrossOver sources ask for this version or a newer one.

